Rootfast — licensing
=====================

This repository ships two distinct things under two distinct licenses:

  - Code (everything that is not data)            — MIT License
  - Data (the unified Rootfast dataset and any
    intermediate caches derived from upstream
    public-domain sources)                        — CC0 1.0 Universal

The dataset is itself a derivative of public-domain federal data (USDA PLANTS,
USDA-ARS Plant Hardiness Zone Map) plus CC0-licensed taxonomy (GBIF Backbone).
We publish it under CC0 so downstream consumers inherit the same freedoms.

iNaturalist photo URLs and attributions stored in the dataset retain the
per-photo Creative Commons license set by the photographer (CC-BY-NC, CC-BY,
CC0, etc.). The `photo_license` and `photo_attribution` fields are the source
of truth for each photo's terms — Rootfast's CC0 release applies to the URL
*as a record*, not to the image bytes referenced by it.

